# The dungeon tileset. Four 18x18 frames, drawn 1:1: wall, floor, stairs,
# unlit.
#
# The first three are in TileKind order so the sheet indexes by the enum. The
# fourth has no enum value — it is the same floor at the bottom of the crypt
# ramp, drawn where the torch does not reach, and it exists because "out of
# sight" has to be a colour rather than an absence. A black hole in a dungeon
# reads as a bug.
#
# Six steps of blue-grey and no hue is the point (see the palette header): at
# 60x34 tiles, value *is* the level geometry, and any real colour in the
# architecture would drown the monsters.
name roguelike-tiles
size 72 18
key a crypt-0-pit
key b crypt-2
key c crypt-3
key d crypt-1
key s crypt-1
key p crypt-1
pixels
